        "id": "openalex:W4387129001",
        "source": "openalex",
        "title": "When Retrieval Fails: Noisy Contexts and Hallucination Amplification in RAG",
        "abstract": "While retrieval-augmented generation substantially reduces extrinsic hallucinations when relevant passages are retrieved, language models remain vulnerable to noisy or contradictory contexts. In controlled distraction experiments across 4,200 scientific queries, injecting topically similar but factually irrelevant passages into the prompt increases unfaithful synthesis claims from 8.1% to 27.4%. Furthermore, language models frequently fabricate citations by attributing true parametric statements to retrieved passages that do not mention them; up to 31% of inline citations in standard RAG outputs fail strict entailment checks.",
